# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A RULE.
#
# Two failures happened in the earlier repos and both are encoded here.
#
# 1. Rebuttals/ added `__pycache__/` AFTER those files were already committed.
#    A .gitignore has no effect on files git already tracks, so they are still
#    in that repo today. Add rules BEFORE the first commit, and verify with
#    `git status --short`.
#
# 2. Rebuttals_2/ ignored `results/` wholesale to keep the tree clean. That
#    silently broke the ONLY channel for getting numbers off the training box
#    and back onto a laptop for auditing. Every run looked fine on Paperspace
#    and produced nothing pullable.
#
#    `results/` IS TRACKED HERE. Do not add it. Its contents are small .json
#    and .md; the heavy things that rule was really aimed at (.npz, .pt, .csv,
#    datasets) are excluded by their own patterns below, wherever they appear.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Datasets: large, and CUB-200-2011 / Places / CelebA are not ours to
# redistribute. They live in a SIBLING directory, never inside the repo.
data/
datasets/
waterbird*/
celeba*/
img_align_celeba*/
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.7z

# Cached representations. Regenerable, hundreds of MB each, and there is one
# per (dataset, backbone) pair so they add up fast.
*.npz
features_*/

# Trained weights. Regenerable.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors

# Raw tabular dumps that sometimes land next to the code
*.csv
*.tsv
*.parquet
# A small summary csv in results/ is allowed through. The comment must stay on its
# own line: git does not strip a trailing '# ...', and on the same line it made the
# pattern match nothing, so results/v5_bird_fraction.csv was never pulled.
!results/*.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
